{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# The completion-verifier close gate FAILS OPEN on an LLM provider error (via the epic-close bug screen)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nClosing epic `e369-a449-4773-48fb`, the completion verifier's epic-close bug\nscreen hit a Bedrock `ValidationException` (`LLMUnavailableError`) on every one\nof its 32 per-candidate calls — and the verifier still returned PASS, exit 0.\nThe screen's `except Exception` degrade coerces EVERY per-candidate failure to\nverdict `C` (\"unrelated\"), so a systematic provider outage silently turns the\nepic's caused_by bug floor into a no-op with no signal anywhere: not in the\nverdict, not in the sidecar, not in the exit code. Contrast: when the provider\npackage is merely absent, the same gate correctly REFUSES the close. Two\nfailure modes of one dependency, opposite outcomes — and the fail-open one\nfires exactly when the provider is degraded. (Full RCA in the comments; the\noriginal \"the outer gate swallows the error\" framing was refuted — the outer\nclose gate already fails closed on any exception from `verify_completion`. The\nreal fail-open is the screen-layer degrade.)\n\nThe prior RCA's other confirmed defect — `max_tokens` never re-clamped for a\nsmaller model, the source of the 400 itself — is already fixed and merged\n(commit `e49e7a418a`, Gerrit change 1361).\n\n**Operator-ratified decision (2026-08-04, recorded in the comments): FAIL\nCLOSED.** A provider error during the completion verifier must BLOCK the close\n(nonzero exit, error naming the provider failure, ticket stays `in_progress`),\nconsistent with the absent-provider path. The escape hatch is the existing\nforce flag (`--force-close`; its rename to `--force` is story\n24f7-1955-bcd8-4f29, out of scope here).\n\n## Approach\n\nMake the epic-close bug screen propagate `LLMUnavailableError` instead of\ndegrading it to `C`, at both layers where it is currently swallowed:\n\n1. `epic_bug_screen.screen_candidates._row` — re-raise `LLMUnavailableError`\n   before the broad per-candidate degrade (warm call and fan-out alike; the\n   `ThreadPoolExecutor.map` surfaces the first worker exception on iteration).\n2. `epic_bug_screen.run_screen` — re-raise `LLMUnavailableError` before the\n   outer \"the screen is advisory\" broad except.\n\nNon-provider failures (malformed output, contract/config errors, store read\nerrors) keep the documented degrade-open behavior — only the SYSTEMIC\nprovider-error class fails closed. From there the existing machinery already\ndoes the right thing with no further change: the workflow interpreter captures\nthe step exception as a failed step, `produce_completion_verdict` raises on a\nnon-succeeded run, and `transition_close._completion_precheck`'s fail-closed\nhandler blocks the close with the standard \"completion verification could not\nrun (…) Override with --force-close\" message carrying the provider failure\ntext. `--force-close` bypasses the verifier before the screen ever runs, so the\nescape hatch is untouched. Docstrings/comments that state \"the screen never\nblocks a close\" are updated to name the one deliberate exception. This does not\nregress Gerrit change 1360 (`_legacy_material_ok` grandfathering, the\ncertifiable=False stderr warning, `certifiable` in the PASS sidecar): none of\nthose paths are touched.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/epic_bug_screen.py` — the two re-raise seams + docstrings.\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_ops.py` — comment/docstring accuracy only.\n- `tests/unit/test_epic_bug_screen_4b54.py` and/or a new\n  `tests/unit/test_close_gate_provider_error_1019.py` — the RED-first\n  behavioral tests below.\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py` — a provider-error\n  close-refusal case at the gate seam if not already covered.\n\n## Testing\n\nRED first (each fails on current main, for the right reason):\n\n- a screen call raising `LLMUnavailableError` propagates out of\n  `screen_candidates` (warm-call and fan-out cases) and out of `run_screen` —\n  driving the seam to RAISE, not asserting a mock's call count;\n- end-to-end at the close-gate seam: a verifier run that dies with a provider\n  error blocks the close — nonzero exit, ticket stays `in_progress`, no\n  signature, the error message names the provider failure.\n\nPinned-unchanged (must stay green):\n\n- non-provider per-candidate failures still degrade to `C`\n  (`test_screen_per_candidate_failure_degrades_to_c`,\n  `test_run_screen_degrades_open_on_total_failure`);\n- absent-provider/missing-extra close still fails closed\n  (`test_gate_missing_llm_fails_closed`);\n- `--force-close` still bypasses (`test_force_close_skips_verify_and_sign`);\n- healthy PASS close still mints the signed attestation per change-1360\n  behavior (`test_gate_pass_closes_and_signs_after_close`,\n  `test_gate_pass_uncertifiable_warns_on_stderr`).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a completion-verifier run in which the epic-close bug screen raises\n      `LLMUnavailableError` REFUSES the close: nonzero exit, ticket stays\n      `in_progress`, no signature, the error names the provider failure, and\n      the existing `--force-close` escape hatch still applies — checked by the\n      new gate-seam test passing.\n- [ ] a test pins the refusal by driving the screen to RAISE the provider\n      error (not by asserting on a mock's call count) — checked by the new\n      unit tests in the screen module's suite passing, RED-first.\n- [ ] non-provider screen failures still degrade open, and the absent-provider,\n      force-close, and healthy-PASS close paths are byte-for-byte unchanged —\n      checked by the pre-existing tests named in ## Testing staying green.\n- [ ] the `max_tokens` re-clamp for a smaller model (the source of the original\n      400) is merged — checked by commit `e49e7a418a` reachable from `main`.\n- [ ] epic e369's close disposition is explicitly recorded on this ticket:\n      either re-verified once the gate works, or its unsigned close accepted\n      with the reason stated — checked by a closing comment on this ticket."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785863008609817001,"uuid":"f19f3618-4f4e-4078-ad10-e2a11852dc2e"}